                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "234850181",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197997788394",
                            "num_reviews": 1971,
                            "playtime_forever": 146,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 146,
                            "last_played": 1479144517
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The time management mechanics feel undercooked: there's no action queuing, so you're stuck waiting for a worker to finish one task before you can even assign the next, which drags the pacing in a genre that should feel snappy and reactive. Builders also move slowly and need to be deployed in bulk to get anything done, while there's little clear logic behind which jobs couriers get assigned, making the whole workflow feel more like guesswork than strategy. On top of the gameplay friction, the storyline is thin and doesn't do much to justify the 55 levels beyond basic task variety. Adding action queuing, speeding up builder pacing, and giving the courier job system clearer logic would make the core loop far less tedious and let the \"rebuilding a kingdom\" premise actually shine.",
